# Wave W17-AA (Route 218): cause floor — lamp-lit plank floor: long warm planks laid along the road over bright water, their joints dark, carrying sparse amber lamp-glow flecks — the design’s lamps drawn in the floor kind’s own art, art layer only (design: the Bridgeport causeway, planks over bright water, lamp-lit in the rain; Revelry behind, the harbour ahead). Converts the shipped boardwalk entire — the causeway method (Ruling #4): a causeway has no banks, so the planks ARE the path tier. Split from the shipped boardwalk it replaces by light entire (lamp-amber flecks vs plain harbour planks) and from Foamline Path’s plank floor ahead of the program by weather: this floor is lit for rain, that one foamed for sun.
